---

<ServiceLayout
  lang={lang}
  title="Websites & landing pages for brands | SEZMOO"
  description="A website is where the rest of the marketing lands – if it does not lead to contact, everything upstream works for nothing. We design and build company"
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLd={[jsonLd, faqJsonLd]}
>
<div class="sd">
<section class="sd__hero shell">
  <span class="sd__kick reveal"><i></i>Services</span>
  <h1 class="sd__h1 reveal">Websites and <span style="color:#ffd200">landing pages.</span></h1>
  <p class="sd__lead reveal" data-d="1">A website is where <b>the rest of the marketing lands</b> – if it does not lead to contact, everything upstream works for nothing.</p>
  <p class="sd__lead reveal" data-d="1">We build company sites, campaign landing pages and shops – on WordPress, in React or in any technology the project needs. Video, photo and graphics are in-house, so the site is not waiting on material.</p>
  <div class="sd__facts reveal" data-d="2">
    <div class="sd__fact"><span>Scope</span><strong>Site · landing · shop</strong></div>
    <div class="sd__fact"><span>Tech</span><strong>WordPress · React · custom</strong></div>
    <div class="sd__fact"><span>Content</span><strong>Video and photo in-house</strong></div>
    <div class="sd__fact"><span>Goal</span><strong>Contact and sales</strong></div>
  </div>
  <figure class="sd__reel reveal" data-d="1">
    <img src="/assets/optimized/lcp/captains-club-ext-ab51c70e-1920.webp" srcset="/assets/optimized/lcp/captains-club-ext-ab51c70e-800.webp 800w, /assets/optimized/lcp/captains-club-ext-ab51c70e-1280.webp 1280w, /assets/optimized/lcp/captains-club-ext-ab51c70e-1920.webp 1920w" sizes="100vw" width="1920" height="1280" alt="Captain's Club" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
    <figcaption><b>Captain's Club</b><span>Digital support / event page</span></figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
<div class="sd__body shell">
  <div>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-overview">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>Overview</span></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <h3 class="fmt-lead reveal">Even the best design is just a picture until someone builds it properly.</h3>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We build sites that look exactly like the approved design, load fast and are easy to edit after launch.</p>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We choose the technology to fit the goal: WordPress, React or something else – depending on how much interaction you need, how often content changes and what the site has to connect to.</p>
      <div class="sd__more reveal"><a class="is-lead" href="#build">1:1 build ↓</a><a href="#technology">Technology ↓</a><a href="#motion">Motion ↓</a><a href="#seo">SEO &amp; speed ↓</a><a href="#integrations">Integrations ↓</a><a href="#care">Care ↓</a></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-zakres">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><h2>What we build</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <details class="sd__g reveal" open><summary><h3>Company websites</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>Profile sites, company sites and portals – clear structure, a sensible path to contact and content that can grow.</p><div class="sd__tags"><span>Company website</span><span>Profile site</span><span>Multilingual site</span><span>Content portal</span><span>Company blog</span><span>Site migration</span></div></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal" open><summary><h3>Landing pages</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>Pages for campaigns and launches – one message, one action, and measurement of what actually happened.</p><div class="sd__tags"><span>Landing page</span><span>Campaign page</span><span>Product page</span><span>Launch page</span><span>Forms and leads</span><span>A/B testing</span></div></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal"><summary><h3>Shops &amp; integrations</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>Online shops and connections to the systems the company already uses – payments, stock or CRM.</p><div class="sd__tags"><span>Online shop</span><span>Product pages</span><span>Payments and delivery</span><span>CRM integration</span><span>Stock integration</span><span>Analytics setup</span></div></div></details>
            </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="build">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>01</span><h2>Built 1:1 from the design</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We move the design into code with no “close enough”. Spacing, typography and component behaviour match what you approved – on every screen, from phone to large monitor.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>Pixel perfect</span><span>Responsive</span><span>Device testing</span><span>Browser compatibility</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="technology">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>02</span><h2>Technology</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We work in WordPress, React and other technologies – the choice depends on the project, not on habit. A simple company site and a large site with integrations need different tools.</p>
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">There is always a CMS your team can use to change copy, images and pages on their own.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>WordPress</span><span>React</span><span>Any tech stack</span><span>CMS</span><span>Multilingual</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="motion">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>03</span><h2>Motion &amp; interaction</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">Animation should help people read the page, not slow it down. We use it where it guides the eye or confirms an action – and keep performance in check.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>Scroll animation</span><span>Micro-interactions</span><span>Background video</span><span>Performance</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="seo">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>04</span><h2>SEO &amp; speed</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">A correct heading structure, metadata, structured data and fast loading are the foundation of visibility in Google. We build them in from day one instead of patching after launch.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>Technical SEO</span><span>Core Web Vitals</span><span>Structured data</span><span>301 redirects</span><span>Analytics</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="integrations">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>05</span><h2>Integrations</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">We connect the site to the tools you already use: forms go to the CRM, sign-ups to the newsletter and orders to stock – no manual copying.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>CRM</span><span>Newsletter</span><span>Payments</span><span>Stock</span><span>API</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="care">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><span class="sd__kick"><i></i>06</span><h2>Care after launch</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <p class="fmt-p reveal">After launch we stay in touch: updates, backups, fixes and new sections. When moving from an old site we set up redirects so you keep your Google rankings.</p>
      <div class="sd__tags reveal" style="margin-top:20px"><span>Updates</span><span>Backups</span><span>Hosting and domain</span><span>Ongoing development</span></div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-proces">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><h2>How we work</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <div class="sd__steps">
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>Workshop</h3><p>We settle the goal, the audience and the content structure.</p></div>
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>UX/UI design</h3><p>Wireframes and visual design, section by section.</p></div>
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>Content</h3><p>Copy, photos and video prepared for the layout.</p></div>
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>Development</h3><p>WordPress, React or another stack, analytics and testing.</p></div>
        <div class="sd__step reveal"><h3>Care</h3><p>Updates, fixes and development after launch.</p></div>
      </div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-work">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><h2>Selected work</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <div class="sd__work">
        <a class="sd__wi reveal" href="/en/realizacja-primespot/"><div class="sd__wm"><AssetImage src="/assets/portfolio/primespot/pjur-blue-wide-2.jpg" alt="PrimeSpot – Landing · Campaign" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[400, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, (max-width: 1100px) 40vw, 28vw" quality={72} /></div><span>Landing · Campaign</span><h3>PrimeSpot ↗</h3></a>
        <a class="sd__wi reveal" href="/realizacja-world-of-warships/"><div class="sd__wm"><AssetImage src="/assets/work/captains-club-int.avif" alt="World of Warships – Event · Digital" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[400, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, (max-width: 1100px) 40vw, 28vw" quality={72} /></div><span>Event · Digital</span><h3>World of Warships ↗</h3></a>
        <a class="sd__wi reveal" href="/en/realizacja-soho-form/"><div class="sd__wm"><AssetImage src="/assets/portfolio/soho-form/soho-fotel.webp" alt="Soho Form – Company website · Furniture" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[400, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, (max-width: 1100px) 40vw, 28vw" quality={72} /></div><span>Company website · Furniture</span><h3>Soho Form ↗</h3></a>
      </div>
      <div class="sd__more reveal">
        <a class="is-lead" href="/en/portfolio-en/#pt-grid">Full portfolio ↗</a>
        <a href="/en/portfolio-en/?cat=video#pt-grid">Video</a>
        <a href="/en/portfolio-en/?cat=animacje#pt-grid">Animation</a>
        <a href="/en/portfolio-en/?cat=eventy#pt-grid">Events</a>
        <a href="/en/portfolio-en/?cat=grafika#pt-grid">Graphics</a>
      </div>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-faq">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><h2>FAQ – common questions</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <details class="sd__g reveal" open><summary><h3>Which technologies do you use?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>Most often WordPress and React, but we choose the technology per project: interactivity, speed, ease of editing and planned integrations all matter. You get our recommendation with the quote.</p></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal"><summary><h3>Will I be able to edit the site myself?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>Yes. Every site comes with a CMS, and after launch we show you how to use it.</p></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal"><summary><h3>What does the build process look like?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>We build the site on a staging server, test it across devices and browsers, then share it for approval. After sign-off we move it to your hosting, connect the domain and set up redirects from old URLs.</p></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal"><summary><h3>Do you design the site too?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>Yes – design is part of our <a href="/en/services/ux-ui-design/" style="color:var(--fg);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:#ffd200;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:3px">UX/UI design</a> service. One team from design to code means fewer handovers and fewer misunderstandings.</p></div></details>
      <details class="sd__g reveal"><summary><h3>What if a bug shows up after launch?</h3><span class="sd__pm"></span></summary><div class="sd__gin"><p>We fix it. Changes beyond the agreed scope are quoted separately before we start.</p></div></details>
          </div>
    </section>
    <section class="sd__blk sd__split" id="sd-related">
      <div class="sd__splitL"><div class="sd__blkh reveal"><h2>See also</h2></div></div>
      <div class="sd__splitR">
      <div class="svcA" style="margin-top:0">
        <a class="svcA__row reveal" href="/en/services/ux-ui-design/"><span class="svcA__no">01</span><h3 class="svcA__t">UX/UI design</h3><p class="svcA__d">User journeys, wireframes, prototypes and design systems.</p><span class="svcA__go">↗</span></a>
        <a class="svcA__row reveal" href="/en/services/paid-campaigns/"><span class="svcA__no">02</span><h3 class="svcA__t">Paid campaigns</h3><p class="svcA__d">Traffic from Google, Meta and TikTok sent to your site.</p><span class="svcA__go">↗</span></a>
        <a class="svcA__row reveal" href="/en/services/video-production-reels/"><span class="svcA__no">03</span><h3 class="svcA__t">Video production</h3><p class="svcA__d">Video for your site, landing pages and campaigns.</p><span class="svcA__go">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="sub-cta reveal">
        <div><h2>Let’s build a site that works.</h2><p>Tell us what site you need and what it should do. We will come back with a proposed stack, scope and timeline.</p></div>
        <a href="/en/#kontakt" class="btn btn--primary"><span class="ico"></span><span class="lbl">Get in touch</span></a>
      </div>
          </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
</div>
</ServiceLayout>
